# The scans themselves. 10.6 GB across 231 files, immutable once fetched, and most of them
# re-fetchable from the portal named in their sidecar. They live in Dropbox beside this repo.
# What is NOT re-fetchable is declared in `originals.jsonl`, which IS tracked -- a checksum
# belongs in version control even when the bytes it describes do not.
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.tif
*.tiff

# Generated pages. Rebuilt by `boc build`; megabytes of base64 thumbnails that would churn
# the history on every run.
boccherini_sources.html
boccherini_incipits.html
review.html

# Local build state and caches
.pipeline-state.json
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Per-machine Claude Code settings
.claude/

# Everything else is text and is tracked on purpose: every `metadata.json` sidecar, every
# item README, every document under `digitizations/`, the structure readings, and
# `.rism-cache/`, so the index can be read and queried without the scans or the network.

# Drafted request letters to archives -- kept local, not published.
digitizations/*-REQUEST.md
